# Specialist routing

When a task clearly belongs to a Nova specialist, prefer that subagent over general-purpose. Wiring metadata (invoke phrases, dashboards, handoffs) lives in `.cursor/agent-system/registry.json` — do not duplicate full agent prompts here.

## Before substantive work

1. Classify the task: single clear domain → go straight to Defaults below.
2. **"Just get this done" / multi-specialist orchestration** → invoke `daddy` ("Use the daddy subagent to dispatch this"). It classifies, dispatches or emits a sequenced Dispatch Plan, and aggregates — it never implements product code itself.
3. **"Who owns X / what's cracked?"** (classification only, no dispatch) → invoke `router` ("Use the router subagent to triage this") or run `py -3 tools/agent_fleet.py`.
4. For a quick fleet-health check without a task, run `py -3 tools/agent_fleet.py` directly.

## Defaults

| Need | Agent | Notes |
|------|-------|-------|
| Top-of-fleet dispatch / multi-specialist orchestration | `daddy` | Dashboard = `agent-daddy`; never implements product code |
| Fleet triage / classification / crack index only | `router` | Dashboard = `agent-router`; report-only Routing card |
| Product change verification (pytest / Vitest / Playwright / browser) | `tester` | After code changes; before claiming done |
| Maintainability / danger audit | `maintainer` | Read-only; significant diffs |
| Full-repository security posture / SEC-NNN | `security` | Not for PR/diff review |
| Docs, MDC rules, agent prompts, canvases | `docs` | Dashboard = Nova Home |
| Warrior Trading authenticated site / Day Trade Dash navigation | `warrior` | Dashboard = `agent-warrior`; not Nova Home |
| HOD Momo scanner data-quality / Warrior parity iteration | `hod-momo` | Dashboard = `agent-hod-momo`; owns `IBKR-Scanner-HOD-Architecture.md` feed UML; never feeds Warrior data into the alert engine |
| Webull-to-Nova widget mapping or selected parity gap | `widgets` | Dashboard = `agent-widgets`; Webull evidence is research-only |
| Trading execution ADR 007 / ledger / latency / auto_live NO-GO | `execution` | Audit-only; `execution-continuity.mdc`; dashboard `agent-execution` |
| IB Gateway login / IBC / API port health | `ibkr-ops` | Loud-warn protocol; never stores credentials |
| General scanner L1 + quote/chart/L2/T&S coherence | `market-feed` | `single-market-data-feed.mdc`; hand off HOD pool to `hod-momo`, UI layout to `widgets` |
| News / catalyst pipeline | `news` | `backend/news/` + News UI |
| Backtest product (Phase E) + VectorBT skill cluster | `backtester` | Metrics-only; skills research/offline |
| PR / branch / uncommitted diff security | Cursor `security-review` | Built-in; never swap with security |

## Continuity-only / unowned domains

If `Agent-Fleet-Map.md` marks a domain `Continuity-only` or `Unowned`, say so explicitly. Prefer `daddy` or `router` to name the gap — do not silently absorb large product work into a general-purpose session. Scaffold a specialist via `tools/create_nova_agent.py` when a domain keeps burning sessions.

## Invoke

Use each agent's registered phrases from the registry (also listed in the agent spec under **Invoke phrases**). Example: “Use the tester subagent to verify …”

## Lifecycle

Every Nova specialist report must end with:

```text
**Lifecycle:** memory=unchanged|changed | promotion=none|<what> | dashboard=clean|refresh-required | handoff=none|<sibling|parent>
```

The `subagentStop` hook (`.cursor/hooks.json`) may remind once if the footer is missing. It is fail-open and never edits files.

## Ops

See `docs/agent-operations.md`. Validate with `py -3 tools/agent_contract.py`.
